{
  "$comment": [
    "Every themeable value the renderers draw with, listed once.",
    "",
    "`id` is stable and append-only: JavaScript sends it, C++ indexes its",
    "resolved arrays with it, and a slot a later feature adds is a new line at",
    "the end. An id is never reused and never reordered, so a theme written",
    "against one release keeps meaning the same thing in the next.",
    "",
    "`kind` decides how a value travels and how a platform reads it:",
    "  metric  a number in points before font scaling",
    "  color   an ARGB pair, or a platform color role while it is unset",
    "  font    an index into the theme's font name list",
    "  weight  a CSS font weight, 100 to 900",
    "  flag    0 or 1",
    "",
    "A color's `id` is the light value's, and the id after it is reserved for",
    "the dark one. A color that is the same in both appearances sends only the",
    "light id and the platform uses it for both, so an unset-looking id that",
    "follows a color is not a mistake in the numbering.",
    "",
    "`layout` marks a value that changes size. Those slots alone form the layout",
    "key, so a color-only change never invalidates a measurement.",
    "",
    "A color's `default` is a role rather than a number on purpose. `label` is",
    "`UIColor.labelColor` on iOS and the existing Palette value on Android, so an",
    "unset color keeps following increased contrast and appearance, which a",
    "flattened integer could not. `inherit` means the platform draws nothing and",
    "the enclosing block's color shows through. `tokens:Class` reads the",
    "engine's kTokenColors table, which is why the generator copies it out.",
    "",
    "Generated into src/cpp/theme/ThemeSlots.h and src/themeSlots.ts by",
    "src/cpp/theme/generate-theme-slots.mjs. Neither output is edited by hand."
  ],
  "roles": [
